itment and the defense  there's a little more muscle with a  mutual defense treaty than there is an  agreement with the Chamber of Commerce  but I but I think beyond that Congress  must have must get high marks for the  changes made in the legislation  Democrats and Republicans I think it was  nonpartisan bipartisan effort to  strengthen the legislation and they did  a good job next question please  professor of political science miracle  from Moscow it was very interesting to  me to hear what's another doll and  representative being told about their  discussion with vice-premier Deng  Xiaoping about China joining nuclear  non-proliferation treaty and so on and  it was very positive moment but from the  other side we have a lot of statement  that United States desire to play  Chinese card against the Soviet Union it  is general oppression with United States  don't try to prevent Chinese invasion of  Vietnam and so on and I'm very I see  some contradiction here of course  now after normalization of relations  with China and after afterward with  China so it's such big interest engaging  American technology American economic  help and so on United States get some no  not substantial but some levers to  influence Chinese policy I could you  give us your question please oh yes I  and I'm interested to know  what is the opinion in what direction  substantially United States will now try  to influence you know Chinese policy in  direction for example to press China to  join non-proliferation treaty partial  nuclear test ban treaty denouncing of  theories of inevitability of war between  China between the United States and so  on or in all right  would you like start sending dog I think  we discussed it earlier I just hope that  maybe we went a bit too far and saying  we'd require that before we would grant  him a most favored nation or whatever  the better trade status but I would hope  that we might ask some assurances from  the leaders of the People's Republic of  China